---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Divider from '../components/Divider.astro';

const lastUpdated = '2026-04-30';
---
<BaseLayout title="now — Connor Atkins" description="What I'm working on this month.">
  <h1>now</h1>
  <p class="meta">last updated {lastUpdated}</p>

  <h2>focus</h2>
  <p>
    PhD thesis on whole-slide image classification, toward an August 2026
    submission. The primary focus through the summer.
  </p>
  <p>
    Running alongside: building <a href="https://tokenwright.ai" rel="noopener" target="_blank">Tokenwright</a>,
    a UK company working on AI-agent harness infrastructure. Becomes the
    primary work after the thesis goes in. Y Combinator Summer 2026
    application landing in the next couple of weeks.
  </p>

  <h2>building</h2>
  <ul class="hand-list">
    <li>the remaining thesis chapters, one careful revision at a time</li>
    <li>Tokenwright, harness infrastructure for AI agents</li>
    <li>OpenClaw, my personal agent harness; ongoing craft, not a project</li>
    <li>the token-economy essay, plus this site as its home</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>in the ears</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>while working</strong>: nothing, or brain.fm brown noise, or
    binaural beats. i can't work to music; i'd listen to it.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>music, away from the desk</strong>: billy strings, since discovering
    him almost exactly a year ago and immediately becoming a 0.3-percentile
    listener on spotify. <em>Away From the Mire (Live)</em> is the current favourite
    song, full stop. standing top four: radiohead, pink floyd, dire straits, and
    now billy. alt-rock and psychedelic rock all the way down, with a long detour
    through 90s britpop and 2000s indie that i still haven't come back from.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>podcasts on rotation</strong>: dwarkesh, lex (guest-specific; the
    peter steinberger episode was an instant listen), all-in, diary of a ceo,
    cheeky pint. ai explained for medium-form. anything elon's on.
  </p>

  <h2>playing</h2>
  <ul class="hand-list">
    <li>tale of two wastelands: fallout 3 + new vegas merged, with a mod pack on top. a shared playthrough with my partner.</li>
    <li>starfield on ps5: some solo hours, waiting to do it properly together.</li>
    <li>schedule I: 100 hours solo, now running co-op with two friends.</li>
    <li>poker: intentionally off. it becomes the whole day if i let it. the point of the poker harness repo is being able to come back to it without it taking over again.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>obsessed with</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>tesla, spacex, xai</strong>: the exponential-progress watching.
    optimus, tera fab, the x+xai-going-public piece. treating the whole musk
    ecosystem as an early indicator and showing up for every milestone.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>american football, specifically the tactics</strong>: chris simms and
    mike florio on pft live for commentary. i care about the play-calling chess
    more than the games themselves. madden's in-game tutorial is genuinely awful;
    i keep thinking about what an ai-native coach layered on top would look like.
  </p>

  <h2>thinking about</h2>
  <ul class="thinking">
    <li><em>whether apps-as-software-alone go to zero faster than i'm planning for.</em></li>
    <li><em>what the half-life of a harness design actually is, once frontier models shift weekly.</em></li>
    <li><em>how to measure the ROI of improving a harness vs. switching to the next model underneath it.</em></li>
  </ul>

  <Divider />

  <p class="now-footer muted">
    the <code>now page</code> convention comes from
    <a href="https://nownownow.com" rel="noopener" target="_blank">nownownow.com</a>.
    i update this fortnightly.
  </p>

  <style>
    .thinking {
      list-style: none;
      padding-left: 0;
    }
    .thinking li {
      position: relative;
      padding-left: 28px;
      margin: 14px 0;
      font-size: 1.02rem;
    }
    .thinking li::before {
      content: "?";
      position: absolute;
      left: 0;
      top: -2px;
      font-family: var(--font-hand);
      color: var(--accent);
      font-size: 1.6rem;
      line-height: 1;
    }
    .now-footer {
      font-size: 0.95rem;
    }
    .now-footer code {
      background: none;
      padding: 0;
      color: var(--muted);
      font-family: var(--font-mono);
      font-size: 0.88rem;
    }
  </style>
</BaseLayout>
